.TH KIDSH 1 "August 2026" "kidsh" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kidsh \- lightweight secure shell for young children
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kidsh
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kidsh
(Kid Shell) is a lightweight, low-capability shell for young children
to explore a computer safely. It offers simple built-in commands for
easy tasks, such as showing colors or days of the week, or taking notes.
It is meant to run in a dedicated full-screen terminal so children cannot
easily leave the environment.
.PP
Built-in commands can change independently of the packaged documentation.
While the shell is running, type
.B help
for the current list. Commands with extra requirements or caveats are
described in
.BR COMMANDS .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose output.
.TP
.B \-e
Exit on error.
.TP
.B \-n
Dry-run; do not execute commands.
.SH COMMANDS
.PP
Here are just a few commands that are noteworthy, require some setup,
or don't work all the time.
.TP
.BR help " (" helpme ", " cmds ")"
Print every built-in command, its aliases, and a short description.
.TP
.BR quit " (" exit ")"
Leave the shell.
.TP
.B beep
Write the ASCII BEL character to the terminal. This may have no effect
depending on the terminal, its settings, and whether a system speaker is
available.
.TP
.B bible
Look up a Bible verse from
.UR https://bible-api.com/
.UE
\&. Arguments are joined with plus signs and appended to that URL.
The default translation is the World English Bible (WEB). For example,
.B bible john 3:16
requests
.UR https://bible-api.com/john+3:16
.UE
and prints each matching verse as the book name, chapter, and verse
number, then the verse text. Abbreviations and ranges also work, such as
.B bible jn 3:16
and
.B bible matt 25:31-33,46
\&.
.TP
.B nock
Evaluate a Nock expression. The interpreter can crash the shell; this is
a limitation of the Nock library, not of kidsh.
.TP
.B speak
Speak the given text using
.BR espeak (1) ,
which must be installed and on
.BR PATH .
.TP
.B news
Show headlines from the RSS feed configured in
.BR rssUrl .
This setting must be set for the command to work.
.TP
.BR family " (" fam ")"
Print the plain-text file named by
.BR familyInfoFile .
.TP
.BR birthday " (" bday "), " birthdays ", " age ", " home
Read the vCard file at
.BR contactsVcfFile .
.B myName
must match the formatted name (FN) of one contact in that file.
.B birthday
and
.B birthdays
show birthday dates,
.B age
shows the user's age, and
.B home
shows that contact's home address.
.TP
.BR printout " (" printer ")"
Send the given text to the system printer by piping it to
.BR lpr (1) .
.SH CONFIGURATION
Optional JSON configuration is read from the first readable file among:
.IP \(bu 2
the path in the
.B KIDSH_CONFIG
environment variable, if set
.IP \(bu 2
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/kidsh/config.json ,
or
.I ~/.config/kidsh/config.json
if
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset
.IP \(bu 2
.I $SNAP/etc/kidsh.json
when running as a Snap
.IP \(bu 2
.I /etc/kidsh.json
.IP \(bu 2
.I /etc/kidsh/config.json
.PP
Packages also ship this example as
.I kidsh.json.example
in the documentation directory (typically
.IR /usr/share/doc/kidsh/ ):
.PP
.nf
.RS
{
  "rssUrl": "",
  "contactsVcfFile": "",
  "familyInfoFile": "",
  "bedtimeHour": 21,
  "bedtimeMinute": 0,
  "blacklistedCommands": [],
  "todoFile": "",
  "myName": "",
  "weatherUrl": ""
}
.RE
.fi
.PP
The
.B rssUrl
setting is the RSS feed URL used by
.BR news .
.PP
The
.B contactsVcfFile
setting is the path to a vCard file used by
.BR birthday ,
.BR birthdays ,
.BR age ,
and
.BR home .
.B myName
must be set to the formatted name (FN) of the contact in that file who
is using the shell.
.PP
The
.B familyInfoFile
setting is the path to a plain-text file printed by
.BR family .
.PP
The
.B blacklistedCommands
setting is an array of strings. Any listed command name or alias is not
registered, so it does not appear in
.B help
and cannot be run. For example, listing
.B nock
and
.B printout
disables those two commands.
.PP
The
.B weatherUrl
setting is the URL of a weather service that runs
.UR https://github.com/schachmat/wego
.UE
\&.
An example is
.UR https://wttr.in/St.%20Johns,%20Florida?format=3&u
.UE
\&.
.SH NOTES
The interface is English only. Output uses ANSI escape sequences for
colors; a color-capable terminal is expected.
